===persian===

شصت سال
از کودکی‌ام دور شده‌ام
در آرزوی رسیدن
هرچه دوست داشتم را جا گذاشتم...
برگردم...
شاید
نگاه مادر
نی‌لبک
تیروکمان
و
تابم را در راه بیابم.
فروردین ۱۳۸۰

===machine===

Sixty years
I have been going away from my childhood
in the longing to arrive.
Everything I loved, I left behind...
Let me turn back...
Perhaps
my mother's look,
the reed pipe,
the bow and arrow,
and
my swing — I will find them along the road.
Farvardin 1380

===lantern===

Sixty years
I have been going away from my childhood
in the longing to arrive.
Everything I loved, I left behind.
Let me turn back.
Perhaps
my mother's look,
the reed pipe,
the bow and arrow,
and
my swing — perhaps I will find them along the road.

Farvardin 1380

===translation===

===footnotes===

The bow and arrow are the ones from the proverb the poet made up ten years earlier, in the
poem he sent to *Gardoon* magazine: *once they have taken your rifle, the bow and arrow of your
childhood does not miss.* Here he is walking back to look for them.
